# Build an AI-Powered Autonomous Web Testing Platform

## 1. Project Objective

Build a web-based AI-powered software testing platform that can understand application requirements, generate test cases using an LLM, execute approved test cases by visually interacting with a browser through mouse and keyboard, observe application behaviour using screenshots, validate expected outcomes, and generate detailed testing reports.

The platform must NOT depend on Selenium, Playwright, Cypress, Appium, or commercial AI testing platforms for browser interaction or test execution.

The core idea is to build our own computer-interaction-based testing engine, where GPT-5.6 Luna acts as the intelligence layer.

This is the first version (MVP), targeting Level 1 autonomy.

Level 1 means:
- Users provide requirements and optionally UI mockups.
- AI generates test cases.
- Users review and approve test cases.
- AI executes approved test cases.
- AI observes the application through screenshots.
- AI determines whether expected results were achieved.
- The platform generates reports with evidence.

Do not implement fully autonomous application exploration in this version.

